From 1a9dbe0abaaf755ffb5fa9c9d3a8fa44b713f27e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 07:44:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Passport section and Profile Completion sidebar not
 saving/displaying real data

- PassportInformation: passport number, country, issue date, expiry date were
  uncontrolled inputs (defaultValue only) with no onChange, and Save had no
  onClick. Nothing ever persisted except the file upload itself. Wired to
  candidate.passport_number/nationality via useUpdateProfile, added
  passport_issue_date/passport_expiry_date columns + migration since they
  didn't exist anywhere in the schema.
- ProfileSidebar: was reading candidate.profile_completion, a field that's
  never attached to the /candidate/profile response (completion is a
  separate endpoint nothing called). Percentage was permanently stuck. Now
  uses useProfileCompletion() for the real number, and the checklist below
  it reflects actual saved data instead of hardcoded static checkmarks.
